arm64: dts: rockchip: enable HDMI-RX on Orange Pi 5 Ultra

The board has an HDMI 2.0 input wired to the SoC HDMI receiver, but no
mainline DT enables it.  The controller, its 160 MiB CMA pool and the
hdmim2_rx_* pin groups are all already described in rk3588-extra.dtsi and
rk3588-base-pinctrl.dtsi, so the board only has to flip both nodes to okay
and describe the 5V detect pin.

Arrived at independently by Armbian as
patch/kernel/archive/rockchip64-7.2/orangepi5-ultra-hdmirx-dts-fix.patch
(pdapandapda <linyuqiang55@gmail.com>, 2026-07-12), which corroborates the
pin bank and the HPD gpio.  This version additionally enables
hdmi_receiver_cma: rk3588-extra.dtsi leaves that pool disabled, and
snps_hdmirx falls back to the global CMA with "no reserved memory for
HDMIRX, use default CMA" when the memory-region it points at is not
available.  That fallback is survivable at 1080p and not at 4K, where a
single NV12 frame is 12.4 MiB.

Not yet submitted upstream: needs a capture test on hardware first.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-ultra.dts	2026-08-23 22:08:57.043880946 +0900
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-ultra.dts	2026-08-23 22:09:31.351555764 +0900
@@ -48,6 +48,18 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&hdmi_receiver_cma {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&hdmi_receiver {
+	hpd-gpios = <&gpio3 RK_PD3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&hdmim2_rx_cec &hdmim2_rx_hpdin &hdmim2_rx_scl
+		     &hdmim2_rx_sda &hdmirx_hpd>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &hdptxphy1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -71,6 +83,12 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	hdmirx {
+		hdmirx_hpd: hdmirx-5v-detection {
+			rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PD3 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_none>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	usb {
 		usb_otg_pwren: usb-otg-pwren {
 			rockchip,pins = <4 RK_PB1 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_none>;
